Spec: NoTeachWeek entity

Purpose:
  The NoTeachWeek entity: one calendar week of a Semester in which nothing is taught. It resembles ../holidays/holidays.sdd's
  Holiday but spans a whole week instead of a single date, so it is stored as one row rather than one row per day. It blocks
  Monday through Friday only, since Saturday and Sunday already carry no lessons. A view-less, route-less package used by
  ../semester/semester.sdd, ../realizations/realizations.sdd and ../lessons/lessons.sdd.

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../semester/semester.sdd

Must:
  A NoTeachWeek has a reference to exactly one Semester stored as a plain id, an ISO week number, the Monday that starts
  that week and a title. The Monday is resolved once from the Semester's year and the week number when the NoTeachWeek is
  created, so the blocked weekdays are computed from the NoTeachWeek alone.
  The blocked weekdays of a NoTeachWeek are that week's Monday through Friday; Saturday and Sunday are never blocked.
  A `fall` Semester defaults to NoTeachWeeks in weeks `42` and `51`; a `spring` Semester defaults to weeks `1`, `10` and
  `22`. Every default NoTeachWeek is titled `No teaching week`.
  @NoTeachWeekService.add_no_teach_week rejects an unknown Semester id with @UnknownSemesterError, a week number that is
  not a week of the Semester's ISO year or an empty title with @InvalidNoTeachWeekError, and a week already blocked in the
  same Semester with @DuplicateNoTeachWeekError, all before storage.
  @NoTeachWeekService.update_no_teach_week re-checks the week number and title for an existing NoTeachWeek, ignoring the
  NoTeachWeek being edited when looking for a duplicate, and rejects an unknown id with @UnknownNoTeachWeekError.
  @NoTeachWeekService.create_defaults_for_semester creates the term's default NoTeachWeeks for a Semester and skips a
  week that is already blocked there, so it is safe to call for a Semester that already has them.
  @NoTeachWeekService.titles_by_teaching_day maps each blocked Monday-to-Friday date of a Semester to its NoTeachWeek's
  title, and lists NoTeachWeeks ordered by week number.
  @NoTeachWeekRepository in ./ports.py exposes list, get, add, update and delete operations backing ./services.py.
  @NoTeachWeekService's `default_title` exposes the shared default title to other feature packages' views, so an
  admin UI can prefill it without importing ./domain.py.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist.

Must not:
  A NoTeachWeek must not block Saturday or Sunday, and must not be stored as one row per blocked date, since a single
  row's blocked weekdays are what keeps the views consistent with each other.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement @NoTeachWeek in ./domain.py with the Monday-to-Friday rule, the per-term default weeks and the shared
    default title
  [x] Implement ./ports.py, ./services.py and ./repository_sqlite.py, with @NoTeachWeekService validating through
    ../semester/semester.sdd's ports.py, per ../architecture.sdd
  [x] Add @NoTeachWeekService.create_defaults_for_semester and call it from ../semester/semester.sdd's
    @SemesterService.create_semester
  [x] Block the week in ../semester/semester.sdd's wall planner and as a single line in
    ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly view, and reject a Lesson inside one in ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  [x] Expose the shared default title through @NoTeachWeekService for ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's form
  [ ] Add the admin UI that edits and removes a Semester's NoTeachWeeks in ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd
